# Preserved source snapshots are hashed byte-for-byte (integrity.content_sha256) and hold the retrieved text verbatim,
# including its trailing whitespace. Never convert line endings and never flag whitespace in them.
evidence/**/_source_text/*.txt -text -whitespace
# Candidate snapshots used by quote_repair.py (sha256 is compared with the re-validation fetch): same rule.
reports/quote_repair_snapshots/**/*.txt -text -whitespace

# ---- Line-ending portability -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `-text` above means Git NEVER converts these files, on any platform or core.autocrlf setting: the committed blob bytes are
# the bytes that were hashed. The committed blob of every snapshot must therefore hash to its recorded integrity.content_sha256
# (tests/test_snapshot_portability.py checks the index blobs, the working tree and the attribute coverage).
#
# The generated / authored JSON files are different: they are written by enrichment_lib.write_json (CRLF, see JSON_NEWLINE),
# compared byte-for-byte with regenerated output, and quote_repair.py records sha256(evidence/*.json bytes) in
# reports/pilot_quote_repair_proposals.json. Pin their working-tree form to CRLF on every platform and every core.autocrlf
# setting (the blobs stay LF; only checkout/add conversions are fixed) so those bytes are identical on Windows
# (autocrlf true/false), Linux, macOS, CI clones and `git archive`.
evidence/**/*.json text eol=crlf
generated/**/*.json text eol=crlf
reports/**/*.json text eol=crlf
proposals/**/*.json text eol=crlf
